  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Let \\(f\\) be a function satisfying \\(f(xy) = \\dfrac{f(x)}{y}\\) for all positive real numbers \\(x\\) and \\(y.\\) If \\(f(500) = 3,\\) what is the value of \\(f(600)?\\)",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{5}{2}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(3\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{18}{5}\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "c",
    "value": "5/2"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12-2001-p9.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Choose \\(x = 500\\) and \\(y = \\dfrac{6}{5}\\) so that \\(xy = 600.\\) Then \\[ f(600) = \\dfrac{f(500)}{\\frac{6}{5}} = \\dfrac{3}{\\frac{6}{5}} = \\dfrac{5}{2}. \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Write \\(600\\) as \\(500\\) times a convenient factor",
        "\\(f(600) = f\\!\\left(500 \\cdot \\dfrac{6}{5}\\right) = \\dfrac{f(500)}{\\frac{6}{5}}\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
